---
title: Grilled Chicken Quinoa Salad
description: Peppery arugula, quinoa, and grilled chicken with a bright lemon vinaigrette.
course: main
servings: 4
time_active: 30
time_total: 40
leftovers: good
tags: [summer, grill]
---

Rinse @quinoa{1%cup} and combine with @chicken broth{2%cups}(low-sodium, or water) and a pinch of @salt in a #medium saucepan{}. Bring to a boil, then cover and simmer until tender, ~{12-15%minutes}. Fluff and spread on a plate to cool.

Pat @boneless skinless chicken breasts{1%lb}(about 2) dry. Season with @salt{1/2%tsp}, @black pepper{1/4%tsp}, and @?smoked paprika{1/2%tsp}, then rub with @olive oil{1%tbsp}.

Heat a #grill pan{} or grill to medium-high and oil the grates. Grill the chicken ~{6-7%minutes} per side, until it reaches 165°F. Leave it alone for the first 4 minutes of each side.

Rest the chicken under foil ~{5%minutes}, then slice thinly against the grain.

== Lemon Vinaigrette ==

Whisk @extra-virgin olive oil{1/4%cup}, the juice of @lemon{1}(about 2 tbsp), @dijon mustard{1%tsp}, @garlic{1%clove}(minced), @?honey{1%tsp}, @salt{1/4%tsp}, @black pepper{1/8%tsp}, and @?fresh basil{1%tbsp}(or parsley, finely chopped). Taste and adjust.

== Salad ==

Toss @arugula{4%cups}, the quinoa, @cherry tomatoes{1%cup}(halved), @red onion{1/4%cup}(thinly sliced), @avocado{1}(diced), and @?feta{1/4%cup}(crumbled) with half the vinaigrette.

Top with the sliced chicken and serve the rest of the vinaigrette on the side.

> Make ahead: cook the quinoa and make the vinaigrette up to a day ahead. Grill the chicken and toss the salad just before serving.
